{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Preserve the existing contents of /srv/inventory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The same two files remain after the repair and restart, with SHA-256 hashes identical to the preparation baseline and executor pre-change observations.","evidence_ids":["prepared-inventory-data","cmd-a248dc19c7c743b6","cmd-c1d61ee32d444a6a","cmd-bb2982593f7a4d81"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Make the existing inventory data owned by inventorysvc.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct metadata checks show every directory and file under /srv/inventory owned by inventorysvc, both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-43d1eacb33eb41a8","cmd-c1d61ee32d444a6a","cmd-bb2982593f7a4d81"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Make the inventory data readable by inventory-readers.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All entries have inventory-readers group ownership; directories are 0750 and files 0640. A group-only identity successfully traversed the directories and read both files before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-43d1eacb33eb41a8","cmd-c1d61ee32d444a6a","cmd-bb2982593f7a4d81"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Make /srv/inventory inaccessible to other users.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Every entry has zero permission bits for others, and direct tests show an unrelated identity cannot list the directory or read either file before or after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c1d61ee32d444a6a","cmd-9c7362576cea4d47","cmd-bb2982593f7a4d81"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve the installed operating-system release and kernel and use a solution compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 9.8 and kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64 are identical before and after execution. The repair used native account and permission tools, with no software-install command in the complete timeline; package health remained good.","evidence_ids":["cmd-13e71c1ae52f4aa2","cmd-9c7362576cea4d47","cmd-bb2982593f7a4d81","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the missing service user and readers group was a necessary prerequisite (cmd-782ae6f381624ca4); ownership and mode changes directly implemented the requested repair (cmd-43d1eacb33eb41a8); and the scheduled reboot implemented the mandatory provider restart protocol (cmd-8ee57ef2fc624f2b). Post-execution observations show no failed services, new exposure, package damage, or abandoned temporary residue. The restart evidence is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, temporary loss of connectivity, changed boot identity, and recovered system, data, identities, permissions, and access behavior, independently corroborated by lifecycle boot observations.","evidence_ids":["cmd-782ae6f381624ca4","cmd-43d1eacb33eb41a8","cmd-9c7362576cea4d47","cmd-8ee57ef2fc624f2b","cmd-69aac46e768a4c4e","cmd-af72c247d772401c","cmd-bb2982593f7a4d81","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct pre-change, post-change, functional-access, and post-restart evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol was also completed and independently corroborated.","limitations":[]}
